FL,308,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30702
SC,0002
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F307A1785953905
OL,3,CUK sees 'really unusual' rise in
OL,4,Chummingbird hawk-moth sightings this
OL,5,Csummer
OL,7,FHowever this year, they say, is a
OL,8,F"hummingbird hawk-moth summer", with
OL,9,Fmany more sightings being reported in
OL,10,Fgardens up and down the country this
OL,11,Fyear.
OL,13,FIf you have seen a moth with a
OL,14,Fdistinctive grey furry body, bright
OL,15,Forange wings, and what looked a little
OL,16,Flike a black-and-white "tail", you may
OL,17,Fhave spotted one too.
OL,19,FDespite being a small species, growing
OL,20,Fup to 6cm long, the hummingbird hawk-
OL,21,Fmoth is often mistaken for a tiny bird.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G2/7
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
